# cv_adapter — Project Context

## Purpose

This workspace fetches job listings tagged "Saved" from a Notion database, scaffolds per-job application folders with a copied LaTeX CV, and provides AI-assisted workflows to tailor that CV and write motivation letters — without inventing any credentials.

## File Architecture

```
base_cv/CV_farzaneh_labbaf.tex          ← master ATS-compatible LaTeX CV (NEVER edit directly for a job), used as a template for all job applications.
base_cv/context_for_cover_letter.md     ← personal narrative and motivation context
base_cv/cv.md                           ← plain-text CV materials, skills, experience, projects, publications, etc.
scripts/export_saved_jobs.py            ← Notion → applications/ scaffolding script
applications/{slug}_{YYYY-MM-DD}/       ← one folder per job application
    descriptions.md                     ← raw job description (from Notion)
    CV_farzaneh_labbaf.tex              ← per-job copy to tailor
    insights.json                       ← extracted role requirements (created by cv-tailor workflow)
    changes.json                        ← summary of CV edits made (created by cv-tailor workflow)
    motivation.tex                      ← role-specific cover letter (created by motivation-letter workflow)
    report.md                           ← CV–JD match report
    position_research.md                ← company/lab research (interview-prep)
    application_fit.md                  ← fit + motivation brief (interview-prep)
    interview_qa.md                     ← practice Q&A; answers + feedback (interview-prep / interview-feedback)
    build/                              ← latexmk compilation artefacts
```

## Key Conventions

- **Never edit `base_cv/CV_farzaneh_labbaf.tex` for a specific job.** Always tailor the per-job copy at `applications/.../CV_farzaneh_labbaf.tex`.
- **Application folder naming**: `{Company}_{YYYY-MM-DD}_{Job_Title}` — created automatically by `export_saved_jobs.py`.
- **insights.json lifecycle**: created once per application by the cv-tailor workflow. If it already exists, reuse it — don't recreate unless the user asks.
- **Truthfulness guardrail** (applies to ALL workflows): never invent employers, job titles, dates, achievements, tools, publications, metrics, or certifications. Only reorder, rephrase, and emphasise what already exists in the CV or in the context_for_cover_letter.md.

## Running the Notion Export

```bash
# Requires NOTION_TOKEN and NOTION_DATABASE_ID in .env
python scripts/export_saved_jobs.py
```

## LaTeX Compilation

```bash
cd applications/{folder}
latexmk -pdf CV_farzaneh_labbaf.tex
# or: pdflatex CV_farzaneh_labbaf.tex
```

Note: `\graphicspath` in the base CV points to the photo/ folder in the repo root. If the workspace is moved, update the path in the `.tex` file.

## Available AI Workflows

Skills live in `.cursor/skills/` and `.claude/skills/`.

| What you say | What happens |
|---|---|
| "tailor CV for [folder]" | Runs cv-tailor skill: creates insights.json, updates CV, creates changes.json |
| "write motivation letter for [folder]" | Runs motivation-letter skill: creates motivation.tex |
| "report on [folder]" | Generates a CV–JD match report.md |
| "rank jobs" / "sort applications by fit" | Runs job-ranking: scores all active applications 1–5 and outputs a priority table |
| "prepare me for interview with [folder]" | Runs interview-prep: position_research.md, application_fit.md, interview_qa.md |
| "feedback on my interview answers for [folder]" | Runs interview-feedback: scores and improves answers in interview_qa.md |
| "export saved jobs from Notion" | Runs the Python export script |
